From 2ef574cc50e96b9499cc9d793f3a7ac147aebf79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:50:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): an all-walled fallback chain at agent build names
 the pin and the earliest reset [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to #3846, which left every ProviderFallbackError on the generic agent_init_failed path. The TUI
build raises a chain only after the pin failed with an AuthError (tui_gateway/agent_factory.py
_resolve_runtime_with_fallback), so the chain that happens is a rate-limited Codex pin whose fallbacks are
quota-walled. That chain now gets the same route_refused card, toast and boundary as a single walled pin:

  ⚠️ openai-codex/gpt-6-luna is rate-limited until Fri 11-20 15:19 PT, and its fallbacks are out too
  (anthropic/claude-fable-5-2 until Fri 11-20 16:00 PT). This chat is pinned to it; use /model to switch,
  or resend after Fri 11-20 15:19 PT.

- agent/model_routing_unavailable.py: quota_refusal_walls(exc, pin_model, now) -> [(provider, model,
  resets_at, kind), ...], pin first. A chain qualifies when (a) the pin is a rate-limited AuthError
  (is_rate_limited_auth_error) with a finite _own_wait (reset = now + wait, kind rate_limit) or a typed
  quota refusal with resets_at (kind quota), AND (b) every fallback is a typed quota refusal with a finite
  resets_at. The pin is named from its chain entry; a model-less entry takes the session's requested model,
  else the provider alone (no invented model). A fallback repeating an earlier route is folded into it with
  the earlier reset. Mixed, no-wait, no-reset and nested chains give None and keep their own error.
- agent/model_routing_walls.py: walled_chain_reply ("is rate-limited until" / "subscription quota is out
  until", each fallback, "resend after" the earliest reset) and walled_reply; a single wall keeps the exact
  walled_pin_reply sentence.
- tui_gateway/session_registry.py: _requested_model (override, else config default) names a model-less pin;
  failure_route names the pin with the chain's earliest reset and its routes in `walls` (single walls keep
  the #3846 shape). Only a chain fills failure_resets_at with that reset (replay clock, client reset_at); a
  wrapped single wall no longer does. Still cleared at build start and dropped from every client payload.
- tui_gateway/methods_prompt.py: card text and its provider/model both come from the recorded walls.

Tests (tests/tui_gateway/test_agent_init_quota_wall_card.py), chains raised through the real
_resolve_runtime_with_fallback with a stubbed resolve_runtime_provider (rate-limited AuthError pin,
SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable fallbacks): pin + earliest reset text, a fallback that resets first, a
model-less pin (requested model / provider alone; and from the session override through the real build),
a repeated fallback listed once, the recorded route with no client leak under the strict contract, and the
turn's route_refused frame + boundary row. Controls (generic): mixed pin, no-wait pin, no-reset fallback,
non-quota fallback, nested chain; a wrapped single wall does not fill failure_resets_at. RED on main's
source (7) and on this PR's first version (7), GREEN after. Changed from #3846:
test_a_fallback_chain_is_not_named_as_one_walled_pin[mixed, all-walled] is replaced by
test_a_chain_that_is_not_all_walled_keeps_the_generic_message (four real-path controls).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
